---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SavingsRateLab from "../../components/SavingsRateLab.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
import Sources from "../../components/Sources.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Savings Rate & Financial Independence"
  description="How long until your investments could cover your life? It depends almost entirely on your savings rate — not your income. See the math that sets your timeline to financial independence."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>What's your savings rate really buying?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Think of your net worth as a tank. What flows in minus what flows out — your
      <strong>savings rate</strong> — is what fills it, and once it's full enough,
      the returns it throws off can cover your spending forever. The surprise: how
      many years that takes is set almost entirely by the <em>rate</em> you save,
      not the size of your paycheck. Slide your income and watch the finish line
      barely move.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <SavingsRateLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why income barely matters</h2>
      <p>
        A raise cuts both ways. Earn more and you can save more — but if your
        spending rises to match, your target nest egg (25× spending at 4%) rises
        right along with it. The two scale together, so what's left over — the
        <strong>fraction</strong> you keep — is what actually moves your timeline.
        Two engineers, one earning $60,000 and one earning $250,000, both saving
        20%, reach financial independence in the <em>same</em> number of years.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Saving does double duty.</strong> Every extra dollar saved is a
          dollar that both grows in your favor and is a dollar you've shown you can
          live without — shrinking the pile you need. That's why the curve falls so
          steeply: a 10% → 20% jump saves far more time than 60% → 70%.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>It's a conservation law.</strong> Accumulation = what comes in −
          what goes out, plus what your investments generate. Spending is the leak;
          the savings rate is the valve. Nothing about compounding lets you escape
          the arithmetic — but the arithmetic is friendlier than most people think.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This is a clean model, not a promise: real incomes, spending, and returns
        are lumpy, and a bad decade of markets can stretch the timeline. Treat the
        number as a target to steer by. Educational only, not financial advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Sources tool="savings-rate" />

  <NextTool current="/tools/savings-rate" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .ss-headline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  .ss-headline-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-headline-value {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .ss-headline-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .ss-stats > div {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .ss-stats dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .ss-stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
